# .easignore — controls what `eas build` uploads as the project archive.
#
# ⚠️  THIS FILE REPLACES .gitignore FOR THE UPLOAD. It does not add to it.
#     When a .easignore exists, EAS CLI stops consulting .gitignore entirely, so
#     every path that must stay out of the archive has to be listed *here* — even
#     the obvious ones like node_modules/ and ios/Pods/. Deleting a line below
#     puts that path back into every future build upload; dropping the file
#     without replacing these rules would upload ~1.4 GB from apps/mobile alone.
#
# Baseline: Android build a6f69563 (2026-08-23) uploaded a 194 MB archive with no
# .easignore present. The bulk is backend/data/cefr — an 87 MB sentence-transformer
# checkpoint plus a 16 MB embeddings array (103 MB of the 114 MB of tracked content
# at the repo root) that no mobile build reads.

# --- The other projects in this repo. A mobile build needs none of them. ---
# Leading "/" anchors each to the archive root, so a future apps/mobile/src/home/
# or .../web/ directory is not silently dropped from the bundle.
/backend/
/frontend/
/web/
/docker/
/home/
/quizDesign/
/.github/
/.husky/

# packages/ is deliberately NOT ignored: apps/mobile/tsconfig.json maps
# @wordwise/types at ../../packages/types/src. Only a test imports it today, but
# it is 16 KB and excluding it would trade a real breakage risk for nothing.

# --- Root-level docs, planning files and mockups (root only: apps/mobile/README.md
#     and the in-tree docs stay) ---
/*.md
/mockup-*.png
/docker-compose.prod.yml

# --- Dependencies and build output (was .gitignore's job; now ours) ---
# A leading "**/" matches at every level *including* the root, so these single
# rules cover both /node_modules and apps/mobile/node_modules. Do not add a bare
# `node_modules/` alongside them — it is redundant, and a redundant rule makes a
# guard test pass after the real rule has been deleted.
**/node_modules/
**/Pods/
**/build/
**/.gradle/
**/.cxx/
**/DerivedData/
**/*.keystore
!**/debug.keystore
**/*.jsbundle
**/*.ipa
**/*.apk
**/*.aab

# --- Local tool + editor state ---
**/.expo/
**/.metro-health-check*
**/xcuserdata/
**/*.xcuserstate
**/.xcode.env.local
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
**/.DS_Store

# --- Python (backend/ is already excluded; these catch strays) ---
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv*/
**/venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/

# --- Secrets and logs. Never upload these. ---
.env
.env.*
!*.env.example
**/*.log

# --- Test output ---
**/coverage/
